1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,885
Before your shift, check the Shared device label on the Omni IC sign-in screen.

2
00:00:05,065 --> 00:00:07,540
Here it says Academy IC handoff desk.

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,539
A named desk helps staff recognize the device they are using.

4
00:00:11,719 --> 00:00:14,129
Sign in with your own account for your shift.

5
00:00:14,449 --> 00:00:18,993
Open Sign-in and security in Settings to check your verification methods.

6
00:00:19,173 --> 00:00:23,056
This example has no authenticator app or passkeys enrolled.

7
00:00:23,236 --> 00:00:29,743
If your department uses verification for shared devices, confirm your setup before taking over a desk.

8
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:33,561
When you step away, find Session in Settings and choose Lock.

9
00:00:33,741 --> 00:00:39,267
A desk shared by an industrial response team or security shift can use the same control.

10
00:00:39,587 --> 00:00:42,232
The lock screen shows the signed-in operator.

11
00:00:42,412 --> 00:00:47,511
This training shift cannot be unlocked here because the account has no eligible factor.

12
00:00:47,691 --> 00:00:49,931
Use End shift to return to sign-in.

13
00:00:50,111 --> 00:00:54,249
Use Switch operator when another authorized operator is taking over.

14
00:00:54,569 --> 00:00:58,751
After End shift, the sign-in form returns with the same device label.

15
00:00:58,931 --> 00:01:01,960
The next operator can start a shift with their own account.

16
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:07,153
This is useful at a search command post or a community outreach coordination desk.
